    "Fix compileExpr(): its string-replacement calls insert the literal text '// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN1*x' / '// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN*x' where a regex backreference like '$11*x' / '$1*x' was clearly intended. The stray '//' starts a comment that truncates the generated Function body, so compileExpr throws on every call and evaluateGeometry silently falls back to the hardcoded default triangle — the equation inputs currently have zero visible effect on the drawn shape.",
    "Change RIGHT_FILL from the pale tan (#fde8b8) to an actual yellow so R1/R2 read as the blue/yellow split the source uses.",
    "Merge the two duplicate 'y = 3' labels into a single label for the shared top boundary."
  ],
  "plan_action_items": []
}

userContent.text:
Here is the generated code to evaluate:

<!-- @FIGURE_UI_BEGIN -->
<label>Wavelength λ on log10(cm) scale: <output id="wavelengthLogVal">-3.00</output><input id="wavelengthLogInput" type="range" min="-5" max="-1" step="0.01" value="-3" oninput="document.getElementById('wavelengthLogVal').value=(+this.value).toFixed(2);update_wavelengthLog(+this.value)"></label><label><input id="spectrumViewInput" type="checkbox" onchange="toggle_spectrumView(this.checked)"> View: <span id="spectrumViewVal">Full spectrum</span></label><span id="demoNarration" style="display:block;margin:0;font-size:10px;max-width:180px;line-height:1.25"></span><span><button onclick="prevStep()">◀</button> <span id="stepLabel"></span> <button onclick="nextStep()">▶</button></span>
<!-- @FIGURE_UI_END -->
// @FIGURE_CODE_BEGIN
var draw = SVG().addTo(document.getElementById('container')).size('100%', '100%');
var W = 1083, H = 347;
draw.viewbox(0, 0, W, H);

var domainMin = -5.35, domainMax = -0.90;
var bandY = 77, bandH = 129, bandBottom = bandY + bandH;
var xLeft = 2, xRight = 1081;
var leftIR = Math.log10(2.5e-4);
var rightIR = Math.log10(2.5e-3);
var boundaries = {
  uvVis: -4.60,
  visNear: -4.20,
  nearMid: leftIR,
  midFar: rightIR,
  farMicro: -1.65
};

function xFromLog(v) {
  return xLeft + (v - domainMin) / (domainMax - domainMin) * (xRight - xLeft);
}
function logFromX(x) {
  return domainMin + (x - xLeft) / (xRight - xLeft) * (domainMax - domainMin);
}
function clamp(v, a, b) { return Math.max(a, Math.min(b, v)); }

var defs = draw.defs();
var arrowGrad = draw.gradient('linear', function(add) {
  add.stop(0, '#fff8bd');
  add.stop(0.50, '#ffc486');
  add.stop(1, '#f36f50');
}).from(1, 0).to(0, 0);

var bandOutlineD =
  'M 4 ' + bandY +
  ' C -5 92 12 103 3 118' +
  ' C -4 134 10 146 3 161' +
  ' C -5 178 10 190 2 ' + bandBottom +
  ' L 1078 ' + bandBottom +
  ' C 1070 190 1087 178 1078 162' +
  ' C 1070 146 1086 134 1078 118' +
  ' C 1069 102 1086 91 1076 ' + bandY +
  ' Z';

var clip = draw.clip();
clip.add(draw.path(bandOutlineD));

var arrow = draw.polygon('306,27 335,3 335,11 807,11 807,44 335,44 335,52')
  .fill(arrowGrad)
  .stroke({ color: '#000', width: 1.4, linejoin: 'miter' });
draw.text('Energy').font({ family: 'sans-serif', size: 21, weight: 'bold', anchor: 'middle' }).center(558, 27);
arrow.css('cursor', 'pointer')
  .on('mousemove', function(e) { showTooltip('Energy increases toward shorter wavelength.', e); })
  .on('mouseleave', function() { hideTooltip(); })
  .on('click', function() {
    showPopup('Energy direction', 'Energy is inversely related to wavelength. Moving left on this scale means shorter wavelength, higher wavenumber, and higher energy.');
  });

var band = draw.group().clipWith(clip);
var segments = [
  { name: 'Ultraviolet', lines: ['Ultraviolet'], a: domainMin, b: boundaries.uvVis, color: '#bd86c2' },
  { name: 'Visible', lines: ['Visible'], a: boundaries.uvVis, b: boundaries.visNear, color: '#d39ac3' },
  { name: 'Near infrared', lines: ['Near', 'infrared'], a: boundaries.visNear, b: boundaries.nearMid, color: '#edc8db' },
  { name: 'Infrared', lines: ['Infrared'], a: boundaries.nearMid, b: boundaries.midFar, color: '#f3b4cf' },
  { name: 'Far infrared', lines: ['Far infrared'], a: boundaries.midFar, b: boundaries.farMicro, color: '#f9e7ef' },
  { name: 'Microwaves', lines: ['Microwaves'], a: boundaries.farMicro, b: domainMax, color: '#dde1d3' }
];

var segmentEls = [];
segments.forEach(function(s) {
  var x1 = xFromLog(s.a), x2 = xFromLog(s.b);
  var r = band.rect(x2 - x1, bandH).move(x1, bandY).fill(s.color).stroke('none');
  r.css('cursor', 'pointer')
    .on('mousemove', function(e) { showTooltip(s.name + ' region', e); })
    .on('mouseleave', function() { hideTooltip(); })
    .on('click', function() {
      showPopup(s.name, s.name + ' is one interval on the logarithmic wavelength scale. Organic infrared spectroscopy uses only the mid-infrared window between 2.5 μm and 25 μm.');
    });
  segmentEls.push(r);
});

var highlight = band.rect(xFromLog(rightIR) - xFromLog(leftIR), bandH)
  .move(xFromLog(leftIR), bandY)
  .fill({ color: '#ffd84d', opacity: 0 })
  .stroke({ color: '#d97706', width: 0, opacity: 0 });

var dimLeft = band.rect(xFromLog(leftIR) - xLeft, bandH).move(xLeft, bandY).fill({ color: '#000', opacity: 0 });
var dimRight = band.rect(xRight - xFromLog(rightIR), bandH).move(xFromLog(rightIR), bandY).fill({ color: '#000', opacity: 0 });

var currentRegionRect = band.rect(10, bandH).move(0, bandY)
  .fill({ color: '#fff', opacity: 0 })
  .stroke({ color: '#1d4ed8', width: 0, opacity: 0 });

draw.path(bandOutlineD).fill('none').stroke({ color: '#000', width: 1.5, linejoin: 'round' });

[boundaries.uvVis, boundaries.visNear, boundaries.nearMid, boundaries.midFar, boundaries.farMicro].forEach(function(v) {
  draw.line(xFromLog(v), bandY, xFromLog(v), bandBottom).stroke({ color: '#000', width: 1.2 });
});

function bandLabel(lines, cx, cy) {
  var t = draw.text(function(add) {
    for (var i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {
      var sp = add.tspan(lines[i]);
      if (i > 0) sp.newLine();
    }
  });
  t.font({ family: 'sans-serif', size: 23, anchor: 'middle', leading: 1.05 }).center(cx, cy);
  return t;
}
segments.forEach(function(s) {
  bandLabel(s.lines, (xFromLog(s.a) + xFromLog(s.b)) / 2, bandY + bandH * 0.55);
});

draw.line(xLeft, bandBottom, xRight, bandBottom).stroke({ color: '#000', width: 1.4 });
var tickData = [
  { v: -5, label: '10⁻⁵' },
  { v: -4, label: '10⁻⁴' },
  { v: -3, label: '10⁻³' },
  { v: -2, label: '10⁻²' },
  { v: -1, label: '10⁻¹' }
];
tickData.forEach(function(tk) {
  var x = xFromLog(tk.v);
  draw.line(x, bandBottom - 15, x, bandBottom).stroke({ color: '#000', width: 1.2 });
  draw.text(tk.label).font({ family: 'sans-serif', size: 25, anchor: 'middle' }).center(x, bandBottom + 22);
});
draw.text(function(add) {
  add.tspan('λ');
  add.tspan('(cm)').newLine();
}).font({ family: 'sans-serif', size: 20, anchor: 'start', leading: 1.12 }).move(0, bandBottom + 10);

var leaderStyle = { color: '#000', width: 1.2, linecap: 'square', linejoin: 'miter' };
var lx = xFromLog(leftIR), rx = xFromLog(rightIR);
var leftLeader = draw.polyline([[lx, bandBottom], [lx, 277], [326, 277]]).fill('none').stroke(leaderStyle);
var rightLeader = draw.polyline([[rx, bandBottom], [rx, 277], [700, 277]]).fill('none').stroke(leaderStyle);

function haloText(str, x, y, size, anchor) {
  return draw.text(str)
    .font({ family: 'sans-serif', size: size, anchor: anchor || 'start' })
    .move(x, y)
    .attr({ 'paint-order': 'stroke', stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': 4, 'stroke-linejoin': 'round' });
}
haloText('λ = 2.5 × 10⁻⁴ cm', 136, 258, 23, 'start');
haloText('= 2.5 μm', 153, 286, 23, 'start');
haloText('ν̃ = 4000 cm⁻¹', 136, 314, 23, 'start');
haloText('λ = 2.5 × 10⁻³ cm', 706, 258, 23, 'start');
haloText('= 25 μm', 722, 286, 23, 'start');
haloText('ν̃ = 400 cm⁻¹', 722, 314, 23, 'start');

[leftLeader, rightLeader].forEach(function(el) {
  el.css('cursor', 'pointer')
    .on('mousemove', function(e) { showTooltip('Organic-IR boundary: wavenumber is 1/λ when λ is in cm.', e); })
    .on('mouseleave', function() { hideTooltip(); })
    .on('click', function() {
      showPopup('Organic-IR boundary', 'The left edge is 2.5 × 10⁻⁴ cm, so ν̃ = 1/λ = 4000 cm⁻¹. The right edge is ten times longer in wavelength, 2.5 × 10⁻³ cm, so its wavenumber is ten times smaller: 400 cm⁻¹.');
    });
});

var readout = draw.group();
readout.rect(222, 92).move(842, 5).radius(7).fill({ color: '#ffffff', opacity: 0.94 }).stroke({ color: '#808080', width: 1 });
var readLines = [];
for (var ri = 0; ri < 4; ri++) {
  readLines.push(readout.text('').font({ family: 'sans-serif', size: 15, anchor: 'start' }).move(854, 15 + ri * 20));
}
readout.hide();

var marker = draw.group();
var markerLine = marker.line(0, bandY - 7, 0, 321).stroke({ color: '#c62828', width: 2.4 });
var markerTri = marker.polygon('-7,0 7,0 0,10').fill('#c62828').stroke({ color: '#7f1414', width: 1 }).move(-7, bandY - 12);
var labelPointer = marker.line(0, 0, 0, 0).stroke({ color: '#c62828', width: 1 });
var markerLabelBack = marker.rect(10, 10).radius(4).fill({ color: '#ffffff', opacity: 0.94 }).stroke({ color: '#c62828', width: 1 });
var markerLabelText = marker.text('').font({ family: 'sans-serif', size: 14, weight: 'bold', anchor: 'middle' });
marker.css('cursor', 'ew-resize')
  .on('mousemove', function(e) { showTooltip('Drag this wavelength marker, or use the slider.', e); })
  .on('mouseleave', function() { hideTooltip(); })
  .on('click', function() {
    showPopup('Wavelength marker', 'The marker is locked to the logarithmic wavelength axis. Moving it right increases wavelength and therefore decreases wavenumber and relative energy.');
  });
marker.hide();

var axisHit = draw.rect(xRight - xLeft, 55).move(xLeft, bandBottom - 25).fill({ color: '#fff', opacity: 0 });
axisHit.css('cursor', 'ew-resize')
  .on('mousemove', function(e) { showTooltip('Click or drag along the wavelength scale to show the marker.', e); })
  .on('mouseleave', function() { hideTooltip(); });

var currentLog = -3;
var organicMode = false;
var markerEngaged = false;
var dragging = false;

function regionForLog(v) {
  if (v < boundaries.uvVis) return segments[0];
  if (v < boundaries.visNear) return segments[1];
  if (v < boundaries.nearMid) return segments[2];
  if (v < boundaries.midFar) return segments[3];
  if (v < boundaries.farMicro) return segments[4];
  return segments[5];
}
function formatSci(n, digits) {
  if (n === 0) return '0';
  var e = Math.floor(Math.log10(Math.abs(n)));
  var m = n / Math.pow(10, e);
  return m.toFixed(digits == null ? 2 : digits) + '×10^' + e;
}
function revealMarker() {
  markerEngaged = true;
  marker.show();
  readout.show();
  currentRegionRect.stroke({ color: '#1d4ed8', width: 2.4, opacity: 1 }).fill({ color: '#ffffff', opacity: 0.10 });
}
function hideMarkerReadout() {
  markerEngaged = false;
  marker.hide();
  readout.hide();
  currentRegionRect.stroke({ color: '#1d4ed8', width: 0, opacity: 0 }).fill({ color: '#ffffff', opacity: 0 });
}
function updateMarker() {
  var x = xFromLog(currentLog);
  marker.transform({ translateX: x, translateY: 0 });
  markerTri.move(-7, bandY - 12);

  var s = regionForLog(currentLog);
  var x1 = xFromLog(s.a), x2 = xFromLog(s.b);
  currentRegionRect.move(x1, bandY).size(x2 - x1, bandH);

  var labelX = clamp(x, 58, 1020);
  var labelY = bandBottom + 48;
  if ((x > 110 && x < 365) || (x > 650 && x < 900)) labelY = bandY - 22;
  markerLabelText.text(s.name).center(labelX - x, labelY);
  var bb = markerLabelText.bbox();
  markerLabelBack.move(bb.x - 6, bb.y - 3).size(bb.width + 12, bb.height + 6);
  labelPointer.plot(0, bandBottom + 2, labelX - x, labelY - 10);

  var cm = Math.pow(10, currentLog);
  var um = cm * 10000;
  var wn = 1 / cm;
  var relE = Math.pow(10, -1 - currentLog);
  readLines[0].text('λ = ' + formatSci(cm, 2) + ' cm');
  readLines[1].text('λ = ' + (um >= 1 ? um.toFixed(2).replace(/\.00$/, '') : formatSci(um, 2)) + ' μm');
  readLines[2].text('ν̃ = ' + Math.round(wn) + ' cm⁻¹');
  readLines[3].text('relative E = ' + (relE >= 100 ? relE.toFixed(0) : relE.toFixed(2)));

  if (organicMode && currentLog >= leftIR && currentLog <= rightIR) {
    highlight.stroke({ color: '#b45309', width: 3.5, opacity: 1 });
  } else if (organicMode) {
    highlight.stroke({ color: '#d97706', width: 2.6, opacity: 1 });
  }
}
function setWavelength(v, reveal) {
  currentLog = clamp(v, -5, -1);
  var inp = document.getElementById('wavelengthLogInput');
  var out = document.getElementById('wavelengthLogVal');
  if (inp) inp.value = currentLog;
  if (out) out.value = currentLog.toFixed(2);
  if (reveal) revealMarker();
  updateMarker();
}
function update_wavelengthLog(v) {
  setWavelength(v, true);
}
function toggle_spectrumView(on) {
  organicMode = !!on;
  var cb = document.getElementById('spectrumViewInput');
  var val = document.getElementById('spectrumViewVal');
  if (cb) cb.checked = organicMode;
  if (val) val.textContent = organicMode ? 'Organic-IR window' : 'Full spectrum';

  highlight.fill({ color: '#ffd84d', opacity: organicMode ? 0.34 : 0 });
  highlight.stroke({ color: '#d97706', width: organicMode ? 2.8 : 0, opacity: organicMode ? 1 : 0 });
  dimLeft.fill({ color: '#000', opacity: organicMode ? 0.26 : 0 });
  dimRight.fill({ color: '#000', opacity: organicMode ? 0.26 : 0 });
  leftLeader.stroke({ color: '#000', width: organicMode ? 2.1 : 1.2 });
  rightLeader.stroke({ color: '#000', width: organicMode ? 2.1 : 1.2 });
  updateMarker();
}

function svgPoint(evt) {
  var p = draw.node.createSVGPoint();
  p.x = evt.clientX;
  p.y = evt.clientY;
  return p.matrixTransform(draw.node.getScreenCTM().inverse());
}
function setFromPointer(evt) {
  var p = svgPoint(evt);
  setWavelength(logFromX(clamp(p.x, xFromLog(-5), xFromLog(-1))), true);
}
function startDrag(evt) {
  dragging = true;
  evt.preventDefault();
  setFromPointer(evt);
}
marker.on('pointerdown', startDrag);
axisHit.on('pointerdown', startDrag);
draw.on('pointermove', function(evt) {
  if (dragging) setFromPointer(evt);
});
window.addEventListener('pointerup', function() { dragging = false; });

var demoSteps = [
  {
    title: 'Read the full spectrum',
    narration: 'The colored strip places infrared between visible light and microwaves. The wavelength scale increases to the right, while the energy arrow points left, so shorter wavelengths correspond to higher energy.',
    state: { spectrumView: 'Full spectrum', wavelengthLog: -5, showMarker: false }
  },
  {
    title: 'Drag toward longer wavelength',
    narration: 'As the marker moves right along the logarithmic wavelength scale, the displayed wavelength increases while wavenumber and relative energy decrease.',
    state: { spectrumView: 'Full spectrum', wavelengthLog: -2, showMarker: true }
  },
  {
    title: 'Locate the organic-IR window',
    narration: 'Switching views highlights the specific mid-infrared span used in organic spectroscopy: 2.5 to 25 μm, bounded by 4000 and 400 cm^-1.',
    state: { spectrumView: 'Organic-IR window', wavelengthLog: -3.60206, showMarker: true }
  },
  {
    title: 'Compare the two IR limits',
    narration: 'At the left edge of the organic-IR window, wavelength is shorter and wavenumber is higher; at the right edge, wavelength is longer and wavenumber is lower.',
    state: { spectrumView: 'Organic-IR window', wavelengthLog: -2.60206, showMarker: true }
  }
];
var stepIndex = 0;
function applyStep(i) {
  stepIndex = clamp(i, 0, demoSteps.length - 1);
  var st = demoSteps[stepIndex];
  var narration = document.getElementById('demoNarration');
  var label = document.getElementById('stepLabel');
  if (narration) narration.textContent = st.narration;
  if (label) label.textContent = (stepIndex + 1) + '/' + demoSteps.length + ' ' + st.title;
  toggle_spectrumView(st.state.spectrumView === 'Organic-IR window');
  setWavelength(st.state.wavelengthLog, !!st.state.showMarker);
  if (!st.state.showMarker) hideMarkerReadout();
}
function prevStep() { applyStep(stepIndex - 1); }
function nextStep() { applyStep(stepIndex + 1); }

applyStep(0);
window.__markRendered();
// @FIGURE_CODE_END

Output ONLY the JSON evaluation object.

systemPrompt:
You are the orchestration agent for an iterative figure-generation loop. Generation works by taking an original static 2D figure, making a generation plan, generating an interactive 2D figure (SVG.js / Chart.js / Mermaid), and evaluating it.

You will receive the critic evaluation, including failure modes, scores, notes, and action items.
Your job is to decide which part of the system is most responsible for the problem:
- planner: the interaction plan or conceptual decomposition is wrong, incomplete, or missing the right elements
- generator: the plan is close to right, but the rendered implementation, labels, layout, interactivity, or execution is broken
- none: the figure is good enough to stop iterating

Use the failure modes and action items as the primary evidence. Do not decide from raw score thresholds alone.
Prefer planner when the critic indicates concept misunderstanding, missing core elements, wrong primitives, or the wrong overall interaction structure.
Prefer generator when the concept is right but the execution needs concrete implementation fixes like labels, wiring, geometry details, styling, or broken controls.

Return ONLY valid JSON with this exact shape:
{
	"next_step": "pass | fix_plan | refine_generation",
	"rationale": "one concise sentence explaining the decision"
}

CALIBRATION EXAMPLES — the decision turns on the failure modes, the five scores, and the notes, so only those are shown here.

Example 1 → pass
{"failure_modes":["Color-Wrong","Missing-Labels"],"geometry_accuracy":4,"interactivity_usability":4,"faithfulness":3,"label_quality":3,"concept_accuracy":4,"overall_average":3.6,"notes":"Interactive elements are mostly functional, but visual and label details do not fully align with the source."}
{"next_step":"pass","rationale":"Scores are consistently high (mostly 4s), failure modes are minor visual polish issues, and concept and interactivity are solid — further iteration is unlikely to yield meaningful improvement."}

Example 2 → refine_generation
{"failure_modes":["Color-Wrong","Scale-Wrong","Interaction-Missing","Camera-Wrong"],"geometry_accuracy":3,"interactivity_usability":3,"faithfulness":3,"label_quality":3,"concept_accuracy":3,"overall_average":3,"notes":"The rendering contains overlapping text, varying colors, and lacks precise interactivity, making it somewhat difficult to grasp the 3D representation."}
{"next_step":"refine_generation","rationale":"The concept is present but execution has multiple implementation-level issues — color mismatches, missing interactions, wrong camera angle, scale errors — all fixable by the generator without changing the plan."}

Example 3 → fix_plan
{"failure_modes":["Missing-Labels","Interaction-Missing","Camera-Wrong","Color-Wrong","Concept-Misunderstood"],"geometry_accuracy":2,"interactivity_usability":2,"faithfulness":2,"label_quality":2,"concept_accuracy":2,"overall_average":2,"notes":"Discrepancies in elements and labels, with limited interactivity and conceptual errors."}
{"next_step":"fix_plan","rationale":"Concept-Misunderstood failure mode and all scores at 2/5 indicate the plan failed to correctly decompose the figure — the generator cannot fix a fundamentally wrong conceptual structure."}
